{
  "title": "Add file logging for pipeline runs",
  "description": "Pipeline runs currently only log to stderr via tracing. When \
something goes wrong (e.g. the stack overflow from #398), there's no persistent \
log to look at after the fact.\n\
\n\
Add a file appender so pipeline runs write debug-level logs to `logs/`. \
Probably use `tracing-appender` with a non-rolling file per run, named after \
the run ID.",
  "status": "open",
